flowchart TB
    accTitle: Public GTA library contribution boundaries
    accDescr: Reusable guides, references, findings and approved generated evidence can be reviewed and merged. Proposed experiments stay labeled. Implementation, releases, private inventory, game payloads and private data stay outside the reference library.
    NEW["Proposed library contribution"]:::hub
    TYPE["Assess material and provenance"]:::gate
    KNOW["Reusable public knowledge
Guide / reference route / workflow
Finding / useful failed experiment"]:::public
    ARCH["Approved generated evidence
Target metadata / exact hashes
Decompilation / disassembly / IDA"]:::evidence
    IDEA["Unexecuted experiment
Label as proposed
Do not claim completed validation"]:::gate
    CODE["Outside library scope
Authored mod/tool implementation
Build packages and releases"]:::project
    INV["Private workspace navigation
Product ownership / local paths
Maintainer's repository inventory"]:::project
    INPUT["Excluded inputs/data
Game executables or copied assets
Credentials / player / production data"]:::excluded
    REVIEW["Review scope and evidence
Attribution / permitted reproduction
Observation vs inference / actual checks"]:::gate
    MERGE["Public library contribution
Commit / push / PR / merge
Knowledge, not a mod release"]:::public
    SAFE["Return a safe reusable method
Without restricted payloads or inventory"]:::evidence
    NEW --> TYPE
    TYPE --> KNOW & ARCH & IDEA & CODE & INV & INPUT
    KNOW & ARCH & IDEA --> REVIEW --> MERGE
    CODE & INPUT -. sanitized method .-> SAFE
    SAFE --> REVIEW

    classDef hub fill:#dceaff,stroke:#245fa8,color:#132d50,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef reference fill:#d9f4f4,stroke:#267b80,color:#153e42;
    classDef gate fill:#fff0ca,stroke:#9a6a16,color:#543b0e;
    classDef evidence fill:#e2ebff,stroke:#526eb1,color:#263963;
    classDef public fill:#e0f4e4,stroke:#367349,color:#1b4329;
    classDef project fill:#ece3fa,stroke:#7950a1,color:#41285e;
    classDef excluded fill:#ffe4e0,stroke:#b64c41,color:#622820;
